    <name>
      <text>Finding Inverses of Functions_9(ii)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the inverse of the function \(g(x)={@func@}\) </p>
<p><b>Hint:</b> \(\ln\) can be typed as <code> log</code></p>
<p>\(g^{-1}(x)=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>To find the inverse of the function \(g(x)={@func@}\), we proceed as follows</p>
<p>Replace \(g(x)\) with \(y\)</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
&y={@func@}\\
&\displaystyle \frac{y}{{@coeff_log@}}={@log(coeff_x*x+const)@}\\
&{@%e^(y/coeff_log)@}={@coeff_x*x+const@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>Solving for \(x\)</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
&{@coeff_x*x+const@}={@%e^(y/coeff_log)@}\\
&{@coeff_x*x@}={@%e^(y/coeff_log)-const@}\\
&x=\displaystyle \frac{{@%e^(y/coeff_log)-const@}}{{@coeff_x@}}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>Replace \(y\) with \(x\) to find the inverse function</p>
<p>\(y=\displaystyle \frac{{@%e^(x/coeff_log)-const@}}{{@coeff_x@}}\)</p>
<p>Thus the inverse \(g^{-1}(x)=\displaystyle \frac{{@%e^(x/coeff_log)-const@}}{{@coeff_x@}}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
